Group of documents, similar to a table in relational databases.

```javascript
db.users.insertOne({
  name: "John",
  email: "john@example.com"
});
```

Unique identifier automatically created for each document.

```javascript
// Auto-generated
{ _id: ObjectId("507f191e810c19729de860ea") }

// Custom
{ _id: "user123" }
```

MongoDB creates database when you first store data.

```javascript
use myDatabase;
db.users.insertOne({ name: "John" });
```

```javascript
// Insert one
db.users.insertOne({
  name: "John",
  email: "john@example.com"
});

// Insert many
db.users.insertMany([
  { name: "Jane", email: "jane@example.com" },
  { name: "Bob", email: "bob@example.com" }
]);
```

```javascript
// Find all
db.users.find();

// Find with condition
db.users.find({ age: { $gte: 25 } });

// Find one
db.users.findOne({ email: "john@example.com" });

// Projection (select specific fields)
db.users.find({}, { name: 1, email: 1, _id: 0 });
```

- `$and`: all conditions must be true
- `$or`: at least one condition must be true
- `$not`: inverts condition
- `$nor`: none of conditions are true

```javascript
db.users.find({
  $and: [
    { age: { $gte: 18 } },
    { status: "active" }
  ]
});

db.products.find({
  $or: [
    { category: "electronics" },
    { price: { $lt: 50 } }
  ]
});
```

```javascript
// Update one
db.users.updateOne(
  { email: "john@example.com" },
  { $set: { age: 31 } }
);

// Update many
db.users.updateMany(
  { status: "inactive" },
  { $set: { deleted: true } }
);

// Replace one
db.users.replaceOne(
  { _id: ObjectId("...") },
  { name: "John", email: "new@example.com" }
);
```

```javascript
// Delete one
db.users.deleteOne({ email: "john@example.com" });

// Delete many
db.users.deleteMany({ status: "inactive" });

// Delete all
db.users.deleteMany({});
```

Improves query performance by creating efficient data lookup structure.

```javascript
// Create index
db.users.createIndex({ email: 1 }); // ascending
db.users.createIndex({ age: -1 }); // descending

// Compound index
db.users.createIndex({ lastName: 1, firstName: 1 });

// Unique index
db.users.createIndex({ email: 1 }, { unique: true });
```

- Single field
- Compound (multiple fields)
- Multikey (array fields)
- Text (full-text search)
- Geospatial
- Hashed

```javascript
// Text index
db.articles.createIndex({ content: "text" });

// Geospatial index
db.places.createIndex({ location: "2dsphere" });
```

Processing data records and returning computed results.

```javascript
db.orders.aggregate([
  { $match: { status: "completed" } },
  { $group: {
      _id: "$userId",
      totalSpent: { $sum: "$total" }
  }},
  { $sort: { totalSpent: -1 } },
  { $limit: 10 }
]);
```

Performs left outer join with another collection.

```javascript
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $lookup: {
      from: "users",
      localField: "userId",
      foreignField: "_id",
      as: "userDetails"
    }
  }
]);
```

Deconstructs array field into multiple documents.

```javascript
db.posts.aggregate([
  { $unwind: "$tags" },
  { $group: { _id: "$tags", count: { $sum: 1 } } }
]);
```

Groups documents by specified expression.

```javascript
db.sales.aggregate([
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$category",
      totalSales: { $sum: "$amount" },
      avgPrice: { $avg: "$price" },
      count: { $sum: 1 }
    }
  }
]);
```

```javascript
// Create text index
db.articles.createIndex({ title: "text", content: "text" });

// Search
db.articles.find({ $text: { $search: "mongodb tutorial" } });

// With score
db.articles.find(
  { $text: { $search: "mongodb" } },
  { score: { $meta: "textScore" } }
).sort({ score: { $meta: "textScore" } });
```

Enforcing document structure rules.

```javascript
db.createCollection("users", {
  validator: {
    $jsonSchema: {
      bsonType: "object",
      required: ["email", "name"],
      properties: {
        email: {
          bsonType: "string",
          pattern: "^.+@.+$"
        },
        age: {
          bsonType: "int",
          minimum: 0
        }
      }
    }
  }
});
```

Documents nested within other documents.

```javascript
{
  name: "John",
  address: {
    street: "123 Main St",
    city: "NYC",
    zip: "10001"
  }
}

// Query embedded
db.users.find({ "address.city": "NYC" });
```

Storing related data in separate collections.

```javascript
// Users collection
{ _id: ObjectId("..."), name: "John" }

// Orders collection
{ _id: ObjectId("..."), userId: ObjectId("..."), total: 100 }
```

Update if exists, insert if doesn't.

```javascript
db.users.updateOne(
  { email: "john@example.com" },
  { $set: { name: "John", age: 30 } },
  { upsert: true }
);
```

Multi-document ACID transactions (4.0+).

```javascript
const session = db.getMongo().startSession();
session.startTransaction();

try {
  db.accounts.updateOne(
    { _id: 1 },
    { $inc: { balance: -100 } },
    { session }
  );

  db.accounts.updateOne(
    { _id: 2 },
    { $inc: { balance: 100 } },
    { session }
  );

  session.commitTransaction();
} catch (error) {
  session.abortTransaction();
} finally {
  session.endSession();
}
```

Horizontal scaling by distributing data across multiple servers.

```javascript
// Enable sharding on database
sh.enableSharding("mydb");

// Shard collection
sh.shardCollection("mydb.users", { _id: "hashed" });
```

Data redundancy across multiple servers for high availability.

```javascript
// Replica set with 3 nodes
rs.initiate({
  _id: "myReplicaSet",
  members: [
    { _id: 0, host: "mongo1:27017" },
    { _id: 1, host: "mongo2:27017" },
    { _id: 2, host: "mongo3:27017" }
  ]
});
```

Operation log recording all write operations for replication.

```javascript
// View oplog
use local;
db.oplog.rs.find().pretty();
```

Fixed-size collections that maintain insertion order.

```javascript
db.createCollection("logs", {
  capped: true,
  size: 100000, // bytes
  max: 1000 // max documents
});
```

```javascript
// Skip and limit (not efficient for large offsets)
db.users.find().skip(20).limit(10);

// Range-based (more efficient)
db.users.find({ _id: { $gt: lastSeenId } }).limit(10);
```

